BC-250/gfx1013: flush the compute TLB by rebuilding the runlist.

The compute TLB on this board is never invalidated.
gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb_pasid() looks for the VMID that owns the PASID in
mmATC_VMID*_PASID_MAPPING, a register that on gfx10 under HWS is never written
-- measured here as 20 of 20 flushes hitting zero VMIDs, and independently
reproduced on separate hardware.

Forcing the invalidation through MMIO does not work: neither the KIQ route nor
the direct register route is acknowledged, and the attempt stalls the
translation unit and resets the GPU.

Measured consequence: hipFree unmaps, hipMalloc reuses the same VA with a new
physical address, the new PTEs are correct in memory, and the GPU keeps
translating through the previous mapping. Confirmed directly -- for 15 of 15
failing pages across 3 runs, the physical address the GPU used is exactly what
that same VA pointed to in an earlier generation.

An invalidation that works does exist on this silicon. A process cannot clear
its own bad translation (60 re-reads, 32 fresh pages, a compute dispatch: all
still 20/20 wrong), but the activation of a second process clears it instantly
(0/20), while merely mapping the same buffer without touching it does not.
That activation is a runlist change -- the hardware scheduler preempts the
queues, rebuilds the runlist and reassigns VMIDs, and must invalidate, or a
process would inherit the previous one's translations along with its VMID.

This asks for that cycle on unmap, so the stale entry never survives to be used.

Result, 36 runs counterbalanced within a single boot, each stamped with its own
execute_queues_cpsch count so the active arm is never in doubt:

  stock     13/18 dirty
  runlist    0/18 dirty      Fisher exact, one-tailed: p = 3.7e-06

Verified active by ftrace, not by a printk: execute_queues_cpsch goes from 6 to
68 calls per run. Zero board errors across all 36 runs, no measurable cost.

Safety: the helper takes dqm_lock, so kfd_flush_tlb() must not call it --
restore_process_queues_nocpsch() and allocate_vmid()/deallocate_vmid() already
hold it, and a deadlock there hangs the machine rather than just the GPU. The
only call site is the unmap ioctl, which holds p->mutex and not dqm_lock (the
same order pqm_create_queue already uses). The helper also returns early if the
device is not a BC-250, if there is no dqm, or if scheduling is not
hardware-managed.

Not finished. Heavier workloads are untested, and preemption under sustained
load is the failure mode an outside report describes on this board (cp queue
preemption time out), which unmap_queues_cpsch escalates straight to
kfd_hws_hang() and a GPU reset. There is also clear room to tune: one cycle per
batch of unmaps instead of one per unmap, or only when a VA range is actually
being reused -- the only case that can produce a stale entry at all.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.c
@@ before execute_queues_cpsch @@
+/* BC-250/gfx1013: invalidar TLB refazendo o runlist.
+ *
+ * O problema
+ * ----------
+ * Nesta placa a invalidacao de TLB de compute NUNCA acontece. A varredura por
+ * PASID depende de mmATC_VMID*_PASID_MAPPING, que em gfx10 sob HWS nunca e
+ * escrito -- medido: 20 de 20 flushes atingindo zero VMIDs, e o mesmo "0
+ * VMID(s) flushed" reproduzido em outra maquina. Forcar por MMIO nao resolve:
+ * nem a rota KIQ nem a de registrador direto recebem ACK, e a tentativa trava a
+ * unidade de traducao (ver gmc_v10_0.c).
+ *
+ * Consequencia: hipFree desfaz o mapeamento, hipMalloc reusa a mesma faixa de
+ * VA com outro endereco fisico, as PTEs novas ficam corretas na memoria, e a
+ * GPU continua traduzindo pelo mapeamento anterior.
+ *
+ * O que sobra, e por que este caminho
+ * -----------------------------------
+ * Medido em tools/cura_por_pressao.py e tools/cura_propria.py:
+ *
+ *   - o proprio processo NAO consegue limpar a propria traducao errada: 32
+ *     acessos a paginas novas e um dispatch de compute deixam a pagina em
+ *     20/20 errada, antes e depois
+ *   - UM acesso de OUTRO processo limpa na hora, 0/20
+ *   - mapear o mesmo BO num segundo VM sem acessar NAO limpa
+ *
+ * Ou seja: existe uma invalidacao que funciona neste silicio, e quem a dispara
+ * e o escalonador de hardware ao ativar outro processo -- despreempta as filas,
+ * refaz o runlist, reatribui VMIDs. Tem de invalidar, senao um processo herdaria
+ * a traducao do anterior junto com o VMID.
+ *
+ * Esta funcao pede esse mesmo ciclo de proposito, no unmap, para que a traducao
+ * errada nunca chegue a ser gerada.
+ *
+ * Onde pode e onde nao pode ser chamada
+ * -------------------------------------
+ * Ela toma dqm_lock. kfd_flush_tlb() NAO pode chama-la: em
+ * restore_process_queues_nocpsch() o lock ja esta na mao, e em
+ * allocate_vmid()/deallocate_vmid() tambem -- seria deadlock, e deadlock aqui
+ * pendura a maquina, nao so a GPU. O unico ponto de chamada e o ioctl de unmap
+ * em kfd_chardev.c, que segura p->mutex e nao dqm_lock (a ordem p->mutex ->
+ * dqm_lock e a mesma que pqm_create_queue ja usa).
+ */
+#define BC250_PCI_DEVICE_ID 0x13FE
+
+static int bc250_flush_by_runlist;
+module_param(bc250_flush_by_runlist, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bc250_flush_by_runlist,
+	"BC-250: 1=no unmap, invalidar TLB refazendo o runlist (0 = padrao)");

@@ after execute_queues_cpsch @@
+/* Ver o comentario longo acima da declaracao de bc250_flush_by_runlist. */
+int kfd_bc250_flush_by_runlist(struct kfd_node *dev)
+{
+	struct device_queue_manager *dqm;
+	int r;
+
+	if (!bc250_flush_by_runlist || !dev || !dev->adev || !dev->adev->pdev)
+		return 0;
+	if (dev->adev->pdev->device != BC250_PCI_DEVICE_ID)
+		return 0;
+
+	dqm = dev->dqm;
+	/* So faz sentido sob escalonamento por hardware: e o firmware que
+	 * reatribui VMID ao refazer o runlist. Sem HWS nao ha runlist.
+	 */
+	if (!dqm || dqm->sched_policy == KFD_SCHED_POLICY_NO_HWS)
+		return 0;
+
+	dqm_lock(dqm);
+	r = execute_queues_cpsch(dqm, KFD_UNMAP_QUEUES_FILTER_DYNAMIC_QUEUES, 0,
+				 USE_DEFAULT_GRACE_PERIOD);
+	dqm_unlock(dqm);
+
+	if (r)
+		dev_err_ratelimited(dev->adev->dev,
+			"BC-250: refazer o runlist falhou (%d)\n", r);
+	return r;
+}

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_device_queue_manager.h
@@ declaration @@
+
+/* BC-250: refaz o runlist para que o firmware invalide o TLB de compute.
+ * Documentacao completa em kfd_device_queue_manager.c, acima de
+ * bc250_flush_by_runlist. Toma dqm_lock -- nunca chamar com ele na mao.
+ */
+int kfd_bc250_flush_by_runlist(struct kfd_node *dev);

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_chardev.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdkfd/kfd_chardev.c
@@ in kfd_ioctl_unmap_memory_from_gpu @@
 			 * dqm_lock livre.
 			 */
 			kfd_bc250_flush_by_runlist(peer_pdd->dev);
 		}
 
 		/* Remove dma mapping after tlb flush to avoid IO_PAGE_FAULT */
 		err = amdgpu_amdkfd_gpuvm_dmaunmap_mem(mem, peer_pdd->drm_priv);
 		if (err)
 			goto sync_memory_failed;
 	}
 
 	mutex_unlock(&p->mutex);
 
